00:00 The arpeggios begin. Notice avoiding the lowest note (programming error in NES)
00:12 Mr. Dudley reads the ensuing harmonies as a '50s Progression (I vi IV V), which I challenge
00:36 Victory topos AKA double backdoor cadence (lol) AKA Mario cadence = bVI bVII I#3
00:48 Loops "from beginning", as customary in game soundtracks
#+end_verse
Deeper floors with more details await in the blogpost down below.

When I covered this with the guitar,
for starters, I had to "double-wrap"
the arpeggio to fit it in the fretboard.
You might want to compare my version to more canonical versions
(such as Harpsibored's example below).

**** The Key is B-flat Major (not C)

[[https://linktr.ee/harpsibored][Harpsibored]] did a nice-sounding harp cover in the original key,
albeit didn't introduce the weird arpeggio "skips"
I'll soon discuss in more depth:
for an audio link see cited URL [cite:@Prelude_From_Nobuo_2022].
Most of the comments do not discuss the skip,
only one does. However, it seems that they
perceive the key signature of B-flat major
dramatically differently from C.
I'm sure it's different, but since it is so subjective
and doesn't really lend itself to further discussion
relating to compositional quirks, I digress.

**** Arpeggio: a Mistake or a Happy Accident?

In the PS1 (2002) and Pixel Remaster (2021) versions of Final Fantasy I
the prelude doesn't differ notably, but the NES (1987) is a curious case.

This excellent review discussing Final Fantasy I soundtrack
is baffled whether Nobuo knew it would later be for the harp
and why it's "choppier" and whether it had to do with the NES [cite:@All_Sounds_of_F_Jaime].

An [[https://x.com/Genki_JPN/status/1957479487555403805][X/Tweet by Genki]] links to a videoclip of a series called
"Nobuo Uematsu special talk show vol.2" and the clip seems
to have originated from a twitch livestream [cite:@Nobuo_Uematsu_r_Genki_2025].
In the clip Nobuo demonstrates with the piano how the arpeggio should start
from the lowest note, but starts with an immediate skip instead, as follows:

